satisfaction and reduced operational costs. [Data: Sources (3253, 3254), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 13), (2024, 03, 21))]", "# ABAP Environment 2508 Overview\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key features and updates in the ABAP Environment 2508, highlighting the new and changed components, their descriptions, and the impact on the SAP Fiori launchpad. The information is relevant to the ABAP Environment 2508 release.\n\n## New Features in ABAP Environment 2508\n\nThe ABAP Environment 2508 introduces several new features, including the ability to view communication management change history in Fiori UIs, the generation wizard for outbound SQL via CDS external entities, and the grouping of events as activities. These features enhance the user experience and provide more efficient development and deployment of SAP Fiori applications. [Data: Sources (151, 152), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 15), (2025, 08, 15))]\n\n## Changed Components in ABAP Environment 2508\n\nThe ABAP Environment 2508 also includes several changed components, such as the deprecated CDS views in business event logging and the log RAP-based C1 events. These changes aim to improve the functionality and user experience of the SAP Fiori launchpad. [Data: Sources (269, 277), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 15), (2025, 08, 15))]\n\n## Impact on SAP Fiori Launchpad\n\nThe new and changed components in the ABAP Environment 2508 have a significant impact on the SAP Fiori launchpad, enhancing the user experience and providing more efficient development and deployment of SAP Fiori applications. The deprecated CDS views and log RAP-based C1 events also aim to improve the functionality and user experience of the SAP Fiori launchpad. [Data: Sources (152, 269), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 15), (2025, 08, 15))]", "# SAP BTP Platform Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on platform updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage technical risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Platform Domains Updates\n\nThe Platform Domains component at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in managing platform domains and ensuring compliance with modern security standards. Their proactive approach, highlighted from 2023, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective platform domain management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 3, 7), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 05), (2024, 07, 01))]\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Updates\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service component ensures that all SAP BTP operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on security and compliance, noted starting 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (2, 4, 8), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 06), (2024, 07, 01))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime component at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in managing Kyma runtime and ensuring compliance with modern security standards. Their proactive approach, highlighted from 2023, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective Kyma runtime management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (5, 9, 10), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 06), (2024, 07, 01))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2023-10-06\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage technical risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2023.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Operational Scope\n\nThe Kyma Runtime Department at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating technical risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential technical pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents technical anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (342, 693), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2023, 10, 06))]\n\n## Java Server and Tomcat Updates\n\nThe Java Server Department at SAP BTP ensures that all SAP BTP's operations adhere to the latest Java standards. Their focus on updating Java Web Tomcat 8 and 9, noted starting mid-2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex Java applications. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technical standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (342, 693), Date_Range ((2023, 05, 06), (2023, 10, 06))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement\n\nThe Root Certificate Replacement initiative at SAP BTP ensures that all SAP BTP's operations adhere to the latest security standards. Their focus on replacing the DigiCert Global Root CA with the DigiCert Global Root G2, noted starting mid-2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex certificates and cryptographic protocols. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (342, 693), Date_Range ((2023, 05, 06), (2023, 10, 06))]", "# SAP BTP Platform Updates and Deprecations as of 2025-08-07\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP platform updates and deprecations as of 2025-08-07, highlighting key components, their environments, and the impact of these changes on the platform.\n\n## Risk Management Operational Scope\n\nThe Risk Management Department at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2020, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 07))]\n\n## Legal Compliance and Governance\n\nThe Legal Compliance Department ensures that all SAP BTP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2020, 04, 01), (2025, 08, 07))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2020, 04, 01), (2025, 08, 07))]\n\n## Platform Updates and Deprecations\n\nSAP BTP has undergone several platform updates and deprecations as of 2025-08-07, affecting various components and environments. These changes aim to improve the platform's stability, security, and functionality, ensuring a seamless user experience. The updates include the introduction of new features, enhancements, and bug fixes, while deprecations involve the removal of outdated or obsolete components. [Data: Sources (1, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10), Date_Range ((2020, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 07))]", "# SAP Technology Updates and Deprecations as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and deprecations in SAP technology, highlighting the importance of timely migrations and adherence to security best practices. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Deprecation of Node.js 18\n\nNode.js 18 is reaching end-of-life on April 30, 2025, and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment. This deprecation is crucial for maintaining the security and stability of SAP's systems and applications. It is recommended that users migrate their applications to Node.js 20 or 22 as soon as possible. [Data: Sources (976, 977), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]\n\n## Deprecation of Instance-Secret Credential Type\n\nThe instance-secret credential type is deprecated with immediate effect, and users are recommended to use the binding-secret credential type or x509 instead. This change is part of SAP's efforts to enhance security and compliance. [Data: Sources (978, 979), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 04, 30))]\n\n## New Features in SAP Datasphere\n\nSAP Datasphere has introduced new features for data cataloging and data modeling, enhancing its capabilities and user experience. These updates are part of SAP's ongoing efforts to improve its technology offerings. [Data: Sources (975), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 01), (2025, 05, 31))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on cloud foundry and technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold technological standards and manage cloud-based services effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Foundry Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in managing and maintaining cloud-based services. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP against potential cloud-based pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. Effective cloud management not only prevents service anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3911, 3912), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## SAP Build Apps and Process Automation\n\nThe SAP Build Apps and Process Automation Departments ensure that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on improving user experience and process automation, noted starting 2023, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex processes and user interfaces. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3913, 3914), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Cloud Management\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Foundry and Technology Departments, established in 2023, ensures that cloud management strategies are technologically sound and that compliance measures consider cloud-based risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating cloud management with technological compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with technological requirements. [Data: Sources (3915, 3916), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 09))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2023-12-21\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to drive innovation and operational efficiency. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2023-12-21.\n\n## Generative AI Hub and SAP AI Core Updates\n\nThe Generative AI Hub and SAP AI Core have been updated to include new features and improvements. The Generative AI Hub now includes prompt experimentation, prompt management, and administrative tools. SAP AI Core has been enhanced with new features and capabilities, including the ability to create and run natural language prompts with a choice of large language models and parameters. These updates are crucial for driving innovation and operational efficiency in SAP's technology landscape. [Data: Sources (3704, 3705), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 20), (2023, 12, 21))]\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Updates\n\nSAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing has been updated with new features and improvements, including the ability to use an additional price type to handle customer-specific prices at the line item level. The Data Access service for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing now also supports OData V4. These updates are crucial for driving innovation and operational efficiency in SAP's technology landscape. [Data: Sources (3706, 3708), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2023, 11, 09))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, and new features have been added, including support for the SAP SuccessFactors Employee Central Payroll connector. Attributes from the customs schema that are complex multivalued can now be edited via the administration console. These updates are crucial for driving innovation and operational efficiency in SAP's technology landscape. [Data: Sources (2871, 2872), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 22), (2024, 05, 22))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and user experience. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Excise Tax Management Updates\n\nThe SAP Excise Tax Management component has been updated to include a new filter Tax-Dependent Material Group. This update enhances the user experience by providing a more efficient way to view data for specific tax-dependent material groups. Effective implementation of this update requires maintaining tax-dependent material groups for master data in the Edit Excise Tax Material Master Data app and importing the latest SAP Analytics Cloud content for standard reports. [Data: Sources (188), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 01, 07))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation component has been updated to include a new feature that allows users to create a Service Instance with a custom Secret. This update enhances the user experience by providing a more efficient way to manage service instances. Effective implementation of this update requires using the BTP Manager to manage SAP BTP service operator resources. [Data: Sources (3688), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 20), (2024, 01, 03))]\n\n## SAP Conversational AI Updates\n\nThe SAP Conversational AI component will no longer be available after December 31, 2023. Licensed users are required to migrate productive bots to the enterprise edition of the platform to ensure uninterrupted conversation experience for users. This update is crucial for maintaining user satisfaction and operational stability. [Data: Sources (3690), Date_Range ((2023, 07, 05), (2023, 12, 31))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting their impact on the company's operations and strategic planning. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Enhancements\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has seen significant enhancements, including the deployment of projects containing all types of artifacts, the introduction of script tasks, and the ability to map custom variables and optional list parameters. These updates have improved the efficiency and flexibility of business processes, enabling users to create more complex and dynamic workflows. [Data: Sources (653, 2193), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 36.0.0 to 37.0.0, introducing new features and improvements. The update has enhanced the operation speed of Preview and corrected the order of component versions in the Marketplace. [Data: Sources (3395, 3396), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 22), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Enhancements\n\nKyma Runtime has seen significant enhancements, including the introduction of support for the extAuth access strategy in the APIRule custom resource and the display of warnings for incorrect Gateway formats. These updates have improved the security and usability of Kyma Runtime, enabling users to create more secure and efficient APIs. [Data: Sources (2196, 1812), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 16), (2024, 12, 04))]", "# SAP Build Process Automation and Integration Advisor Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Build Process Automation and Integration Advisor, highlighting their key features, updates, and capabilities. The information is relevant to the technology landscape as of 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has introduced several updates, including the vertical layout in the process editor, which offers advantages such as drag-and-drop functionality, embedded help, and improved process visualization. These updates aim to enhance user experience and streamline process automation. [Data: Sources (309), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 22), (2024, 01, 21))]\n\n## Integration Advisor Updates\n\nIntegration Advisor has also introduced several updates, including the display of xsd:nillable value in a MIG, support for xsd:nillable in Custom Messages, and software version updates. These updates aim to improve integration capabilities and support for custom messages. [Data: Sources (3632, 3633, 3634, 3635), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 20), (2024, 01, 20))]\n\n## New Features in Integration Advisor\n\nIntegration Advisor has introduced new features, including the support of xsd:nillable in Custom Messages, software version updates, and the addition of new rules for Migration Assessment. These updates aim to enhance integration capabilities and support for custom messages. [Data: Sources (3632, 3633, 3634, 3635, 3637, 3638), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 20), (2024, 01, 20))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and user experience. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has been updated with new features and enhancements, including process visibility, cluster view, and business events. These updates aim to improve process performance and user experience. Effective process automation not only streamlines operations but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (293, 3914, 3915), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 07, 12))]\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Updates\n\nSAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing has been updated with new features and enhancements, including data access service support for OData V4, deletion of all regular prices, and deletion of promotions. These updates aim to improve user experience and operational efficiency. Effective promotion pricing not only supports the company's revenue growth but also enhances customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (3919, 3920, 1759), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 09), (2024, 12, 13))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have been updated with new features and enhancements, including off-cycle upgrade, meta attribute mapping reordered, and regular upgrade. These updates aim to improve user experience and operational efficiency. Effective identity services not only support the company's security and compliance but also enhance user satisfaction. [Data: Sources (1747, 374, 375), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 13), (2025, 07, 29))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of June 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting new features, enhancements, and releases across various components and environments. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of June 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has seen significant updates in April and May 2024, with the addition of 7 new content packages. These packages include learning content, business solutions, and updates to the SAP S/4HANA Cloud. The updates aim to improve the user experience and operational efficiency within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (293), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 05, 31))]\n\n## SAP Translation Hub Enhancements\n\nSAP Translation Hub has received enhancements in June 2024, allowing for the import of ABAP object lists and translation of ABAP short text objects in source languages other than English. These updates aim to improve the translation process and user experience within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (2802, 2803), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 30))]\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Updates\n\nSAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing has seen significant updates in 2022 and 2024, including enhancements to the Maintain Promotions app, extension points for customized promotion master data validations, and new attributes for identifying last calculation-relevant changes in regular prices and promotions. These updates aim to improve the user experience and operational efficiency within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (2804, 2805, 2806), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 30))]\n\n## UI Theme Designer Updates\n\nUI Theme Designer has received updates in January and June 2024, including base theming content for CF and Neo environments. These updates aim to improve the user experience and operational efficiency within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (2808), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 30))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has seen significant updates in June 2024, including the integration of SAML and OIDC logout flows and the addition of application-specific groups. These updates aim to improve the user experience and operational efficiency within the SAP ecosystem. [Data: Sources (2809, 2810), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 30))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of April 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, focusing on various components and their environments, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance the SAP Business Technology Platform and SAP BTP, Neo Environment. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation component at SAP plays a pivotal role in automating business processes. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential process pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. Effective process automation not only prevents anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (783, 3169), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 08))]\n\n## SAP Translation Hub Updates\n\nThe SAP Translation Hub component ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set 